  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Adding Large Transductive Datasets with On-Disk Processing\n",
    "\n",
    "This tutorial shows how to add and use large transductive datasets (single large graph) that exceed RAM capacity using TopoBench's on-disk infrastructure."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Why On-Disk for Transductive?\n",
    "\n",
    "Traditional in-memory preprocessing enumerates ALL structures for the entire graph:\n",
    "- **Problem**: Large graph → millions of triangles → RAM exhaustion (OOM)\n",
    "- **Solution**: On-disk streaming enumeration + on-demand queries → constant memory\n",
    "\n",
    "**Use on-disk when:**\n",
    "- Graph has many nodes (>10,000)\n",
    "- High degreOnDiskTransductivePreprocessors)\n",
    "- Social networks, citation networks, molecular graphs\n",
    "- Limited RAM (<8GB)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Create Your Dataset Class\n",
    "\n",
    "For transductive, create a single large graph:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import networkx as nx\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "from torch_geometric.data import Data, InMemoryDataset\n",
    "from torch_geometric.io import fs\n",
    "from omegaconf import DictConfig\n",
    "import os.path as osp\n",
    "\n",
    "class MyLargeTransductiveDataset(InMemoryDataset):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Your custom large transductive dataset (single graph).\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __init__(self, root, name, parameters: DictConfig):\n",
    "        self.name = name\n",
    "        self.parameters = parameters\n",
    "        super().__init__(root)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Load processed data\n",
    "        out = fs.torch_load(self.processed_paths[0])\n",
    "        if len(out) == 4:\n",
    "            data, self.slices, self.sizes, data_cls = out\n",
    "            self.data = data_cls.from_dict(data) if isinstance(data, dict) else data\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            data, self.slices, self.sizes = out\n",
    "            self.data = data\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def raw_file_names(self):\n",
    "        return []  # Implement if downloading\n",
    "    \n",
    "    @property\n",
    "    def processed_file_names(self):\n",
    "        return \"data.pt\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def download(self):\n",
    "        pass  # Implement your download logic\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def process(self):\n",
    "        \"\"\"Generate/load your large graph here.\"\"\"\n",
    "        # Example: Generate a large synthetic graph\n",
    "        G = nx.watts_strogatz_graph(\n",
    "            n=self.parameters.num_nodes,\n",
    "            k=self.parameters.degree,\n",
    "            p=0.5,\n",
    "            seed=42\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Convert to PyG Data\n",
    "        edges = list(G.edges())\n",
    "        edge_index = torch.tensor(edges, dtype=torch.long).t()\n",
    "        edge_index = torch.cat([edge_index, edge_index[[1, 0]]], dim=1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        x = torch.randn(self.parameters.num_nodes, self.parameters.num_features)\n",
    "        y = torch.randint(0, self.parameters.num_classes, (self.parameters.num_nodes,))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Transductive masks\n",
    "        n = self.parameters.num_nodes\n",
    "        train_mask = torch.zeros(n, dtype=torch.bool)\n",
    "        val_mask = torch.zeros(n, dtype=torch.bool)\n",
    "        test_mask = torch.zeros(n, dtype=torch.bool)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        train_mask[:int(0.6*n)] = True\n",
    "        val_mask[int(0.6*n):int(0.8*n)] = True\n",
    "        test_mask[int(0.8*n):] = True\n",
    "        \n",
    "        data = Data(\n",
    "            x=x,\n",
    "            edge_index=edge_index,\n",
    "            y=y,\n",
    "            num_nodes=n,\n",
    "            train_mask=train_mask,\n",
    "            val_mask=val_mask,\n",
    "            test_mask=test_mask\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # For transductive, wrap single graph in list\n",
    "        data_list = [data]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Collate and save\n",
    "        self.data, self.slices = self.collate(data_list)\n",
    "        fs.torch_save(\n",
    "            (self._data.to_dict(), self.slices, {}, self._data.__class__),\n",
    "            self.processed_paths[0]\n",
    "        )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Create Your Loader"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from topobench.data.loaders.base import AbstractLoader\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "class MyLargeTransductiveLoader(AbstractLoader):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Loader for your custom transductive dataset.\"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __init__(self, parameters: DictConfig):\n",
    "        super().__init__(parameters)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def load_dataset(self):\n",
    "        dataset = MyLargeTransductiveDataset(\n",
    "            root=str(self.root_data_dir),\n",
    "            name=self.parameters.data_name,\n",
    "            parameters=self.parameters\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        return dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Use On-Disk Processing\n",
    "\n",
    "Key difference: Use `OnDiskTransductiveDataset` which builds an index and allows on-demand queries:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from omegaconf import OmegaConf\n",
    "from topobench.data.preprocessor.ondisk_transductive import OnDiskTransductiveDataset\n",
    "\n",
    "# Configure your dataset\n",
    "loader_config = OmegaConf.create({\n",
    "    \"data_dir\": \"./data/\",\n",
    "    \"data_name\": \"MyLargeTransductive\",\n",
    "    \"num_nodes\": 15000,\n",
    "    \"degree\": 60,\n",
    "    \"num_features\": 16,\n",
    "    \"num_classes\": 10\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load dataset\n",
    "loader = MyLargeTransductiveLoader(loader_config)\n",
    "dataset, dataset_dir = loader.load()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Get the single graph\n",
    "data = dataset[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded graph: {data.num_nodes} nodes, {data.edge_index.shape[1]//2} edges\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Use ON-DISK preprocessing (constant memory!)\n",
    "ondisk_dataset = OnDiskTransductiveDataset(\n",
    "    graph_data=data,\n",
    "    data_dir=\"./tmp/ondisk_transductive\",\n",
    "    max_structure_size=3,  # Include triangles\n",
    "    force_rebuild=False\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Build the index (streams to disk)\n",
    "ondisk_dataset.build_index()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"✓ Index built: {ondisk_dataset.num_structures:,} triangles\")\n",
    "print(\"  Memory: Constant (~50-100MB)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Query Structures On-Demand\n",
    "\n",
    "The key feature: query structures only for nodes you need:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Query structures for a batch of nodes\n",
    "node_indices = list(range(1000))  # First 1000 nodes\n",
    "structures = ondisk_dataset.query_batch(node_indices, fully_contained=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Queried {len(structures)} structures for {len(node_indices)} nodes\")\n",
    "print(\"(Only loaded what we need - constant memory!)\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Train Your Model\n",
    "\n",
    "For transductive learning, typically use the full graph:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pytorch_lightning as pl\n",
    "from topobench.nn.encoders import AllCellFeatureEncoder\n",
    "from topobench.nn.backbones.simplicial.sccnn import SCCNNCustom\n",
    "from topobench.nn.wrappers import SCCNNWrapper\n",
    "from topobench.nn.readouts import PropagateSignalDown\n",
    "from topobench.loss import TBLoss\n",
    "from topobench.evaluator import TBEvaluator\n",
    "from topobench.optimizer import TBOptimizer\n",
    "from topobench.model import TBModel\n",
    "from topobench.dataloader import TBDataloader\n",
    "\n",
    "# Setup model\n",
    "HIDDEN_DIM = 32\n",
    "OUT_CHANNELS = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "feature_encoder = AllCellFeatureEncoder(\n",
    "    in_channels=[16, 16, 16],\n",
    "    out_channels=HIDDEN_DIM,\n",
    "    selected_dimensions=[0, 1, 2]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "backbone = SCCNNCustom(\n",
    "    in_channels_all=[HIDDEN_DIM]*3,\n",
    "    hidden_channels_all=[HIDDEN_DIM]*3,\n",
    "    conv_order=1,\n",
    "    sc_order=3,\n",
    "    n_layers=1\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "backbone_wrapper = SCCNNWrapper(backbone, out_channels=HIDDEN_DIM, num_cell_dimensions=3)\n",
    "\n",
    "readout = PropagateSignalDown(\n",
    "    num_cell_dimensions=3,\n",
    "    hidden_dim=HIDDEN_DIM,\n",
    "    out_channels=OUT_CHANNELS,\n",
    "    task_level=\"node\",  # Node classification\n",
    "    pooling_type=\"sum\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "loss = TBLoss(OmegaConf.create({\"dataset_loss\": {\"task\": \"classification\", \"loss_type\": \"cross_entropy\"}}))\n",
    "evaluator = TBEvaluator(OmegaConf.create({\"task\": \"classification\", \"num_classes\": OUT_CHANNELS, \"metrics\": [\"accuracy\"]}))\n",
    "optimizer = TBOptimizer(OmegaConf.create({\"optimizer_id\": \"Adam\", \"parameters\": {\"lr\": 0.01}}))\n",
    "\n",
    "model = TBModel(\n",
    "    backbone=backbone_wrapper,\n",
    "    readout=readout,\n",
    "    loss=loss,\n",
    "    feature_encoder=feature_encoder,\n",
    "    evaluator=evaluator,\n",
    "    optimizer=optimizer\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create dataloader (for transductive, batch_size=1)\n",
    "train_dataset = [ondisk_dataset]\n",
    "datamodule = TBDataloader(train_dataset, train_dataset, train_dataset, batch_size=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train\n",
    "trainer = pl.Trainer(max_epochs=10, accelerator=\"cpu\")\n",
    "trainer.fit(model, datamodule)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"✅ Training complete with on-disk dataset!\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Clean up\n",
    "ondisk_dataset.close()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key Differences: In-Memory vs On-Disk\n",
    "\n",
    "| Aspect | In-Memory (`PreProcessor`) | On-Disk (`OnDiskTransductiveDataset`) |\n",
    "|--------|---------------------------|---------------------------------------|\n",
    "| **Memory** | All structures in RAM | Constant (~50-100MB) |\n",
    "| **Preprocessing** | Enumerate all at once | Stream to SQLite index |\n",
    "| **Querying** | All loaded | On-demand via `query_batch()` |\n",
    "| **Disk Usage** | Minimal | SQLite index on disk |\n",
    "| **Speed** | Fast (all in RAM) | Slightly slower (disk I/O) |\n",
    "| **Scalability** | Limited by RAM | Limited by disk |\n",
    "| **Use When** | Small graphs (<5K nodes) | Large graphs (>10K nodes) |\n",
    "\n",
    "## Example: Real-World Sizes\n",
    "\n",
    "**When to use on-disk:**\n",
    "- **Cora**: 2,708 nodes → In-memory OK\n",
    "- **PubMed**: 19,717 nodes → **Use on-disk**\n",
    "- **Reddit**: 232,965 nodes → **Definitely on-disk**\n",
    "- **ogbn-arxiv**: 169,343 nodes → **On-disk required**\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Create dataset class** (single large graph)\n",
    "2. **Create loader** (inherit `AbstractLoader`)\n",
    "3. **Use `OnDiskTransductiveDataset`** with `build_index()`\n",
    "4. **Query on-demand** with `query_batch()`\n",
    "5. **Train normally** - rest of workflow unchanged!\n",
    "\n",
    "**Result**: Train on graphs with millions of nodes and structures! 🎊"
   ]
  }
